{
 "text": [
  "About",
  "Robots",
  "Outreach",
  "Resources",
  "ABOUT US",
  "Ultro began as Browning Robotics in 2015 when the founders, Robert, Ben, and Gabe, won a robotics competition at Johns Hopkins. With this momentum, we started FTC in 2015/2016 with FIRST RES-Q.",
  "History",
  "2015",
  "Rookie Season",
  "Browning Robotics kicks off its rookie season, FIRST RES-Q. We end up making it to the finals on our very first qualifier!",
  "2016",
  "Ultro Robotics",
  "Browning Robotics gets renamed to Ultro - a testament to our student-driven, autonomous designs.",
  "2017",
  "NYC Championships",
  "Ultro makes it to NYC Championships for the first time in our sophomore season, Velocity Vortex.",
  "2020",
  "Worlds",
  "Ultro makes it through NYC Championships undefeated, winning Inspire 2",
  "nd",
  "and the Control Award. The FTC World Championship was unfortunately cancelled due to COVID-19.",
  "2025",
  "10 Years",
  "To commemorate our 10-year anniversary, Ultro unveils a refreshed website and identity, and launches community team",
  "Ex Nihilo.",
  "Sponsors",
  "Our affiliation with an all-boys independent school engenders a misconception that we have unlimited resources and support.",
  "Ultro is entirely self-funded.",
  "Our finances are also handled by the students to increase our fiscal responsibility and truly be a team",
  "of its own mind.",
  "Thank you to our past sponsors:",
  "337 EAST 64TH STREET",
  "NEW YORK, NY 10065",
  "Ultro Robotics is the Browning School's premier FTC robotics team.",
  "This website is",
  "open source!"
 ],
